<title>JAPAN: Japan real estate shares rise on recovery hopes.</title>
<headline>Japan real estate shares rise on recovery hopes.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan real estate shares rose in the Tuesday afternoon session, lifted by hopes that land liquidity was on the road to recovery and that land prices had bottomed out, brokers said.</p>
<p>They added that dealers were also playing an active part in trade of real estate shares, which topped the list of gaining sectors.</p>
<p>Mitsui Fudosan Co Ltd added 60 yen to 1,530, Mitsubishi Estate Co Ltd rose 60 yen to 1,690 and Tokyu Land Corp climbed 24 yen to 517.</p>
